  "id": "cff",
  "term": "CFF",
  "definition": "CFF refers to a cue-driven feature fusion approach used in time series forecasting, where language-based semantic cues are combined with numerical sequence features to guide predictions. In the source, it is described as a parameter-efficient method for adapting forecasting models by using text-derived information to modulate numerical outputs.",
